# No OKD References

This project documents **Red Hat OpenShift** only. Never mention OKD, link to okd.io, or copy OKD-branded wording.

## Forbidden

- The string `OKD` (any casing: OKD, Okd, okd) in prose, titles, comments, or metadata
- Any URL or hostname containing `okd.io` (including `docs.okd.io`, subpaths, and redirects)
- Phrases that treat OKD as this guide's product (e.g. "In OKD…", "OKD cluster")

## Required instead

- Product name: **OpenShift** / **OpenShift Container Platform**
- Official docs: `https://docs.redhat.com/...` (prefer `openshift_container_platform/latest/...` paths used elsewhere in this repo)

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD -->
[About network policy](https://docs.okd.io/latest/networking/network_security/network_policy/about-network-policy.html)

<!-- ✅ GOOD -->
[About network policy](https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/latest/html/network_security/about-network-policy)
```

## When writing or editing

1. Do not use content that still says OKD.
2. If a search or fetch returns okd.io pages, translate links to the matching docs.redhat.com topic before citing them in the repo.
3. If you find an existing OKD / okd.io reference while editing, replace it in the same change.
